      "cause": "At 132px, Destination has 111px of text space, enough for Metro Manila but not Greater Luzon on one line. The 289px Conditions column has 268px of text space, so its prose determines the row heights."
    },
    {
      "design": "r2B",
      "good": "The wider Conditions column makes the prose easier to scan and reduces several rows to six lines. Windows and headers remain intact, and the table retains clear row boundaries.",
      "problems": "Metro Manila and Greater Luzon both split across two lines, and Remote island areas occupies three, weakening the destination column as a quick index. The first column feels cramped beside the expansive conditions.",
      "cause": "The 113px Destination column leaves only 92px for text. Moving those 19px to Conditions gives it 287px of text space and improves prose wrapping."
    },
    {
      "design": "r2C",
      "good": "Every destination appears on one line, giving the row labels a clear, consistent rhythm. The delivery windows and all headers also remain intact.",
      "problems": "Conditions are broken into many short lines, including an awkward break within the hyphenated roll-on/roll-off expression. The resulting tall rows leave large empty areas under the short destination and window entries and make comparisons across rows harder.",
      "cause": "The 182px Destination column is wide enough for the longest label on one line, but leaves Conditions only 239px, or 218px of text space."
    }
  ],
